IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT domain
IMPORT `g3-nouns`
IMPORT `g3-art8-register`

-- g3-art9-restricted-section.l4: Article 9 (Restricted section): what is public about a restricted-section charity (9(1)), who may request entry and on what condition (9(2)),
-- what the Minister's Order must contain (9(3)), what the request must be (9(4), 9(5)), when the Commissioner may enter the charity (9(6)) and what follows a refusal (9(7)).
-- The content of the Order under Article 9 (the funding condition, the other conditions, the grounds, what soliciting and a donation are, who the general public is) is an input:
-- no Order is among the sources, and the Law defers "solicit" and "donation" (Article 1) to it.  Every satisfaction of the Commissioner is an input.

§ `Article 9 -- Restricted section`

§§ `Article 9(1): the public elements of the restricted section`

-- The matters of 9(1)(b) are those of Article 8(3)(a), (e), (f), (j) and (k).  Item (k) is a public element only if it is registered, i.e. if a notice is to be noted (F3.8).
-- src:255 | (1) For the purpose of Article 10 the public elements of the restricted section are, in relation to each charity registered in that section –
-- src:256 | (a) the registration number (but not the registered name) of the charity;
-- src:257 | (b) the matters registered under sub-paragraphs (a), (e), (f), (j) and (k) of Article 8(3);
-- src:258 | (c) a summary, produced by the charity, to the satisfaction of the Commissioner, of the reasons for registration of the charity in the restricted section; and
-- src:259 | (d) any other element that may be prescribed by the Minister by Order.
@ref Article 9(1) (src:255-259)
@export The public elements of the restricted section for a charity registered in it (Article 9(1)): the registration number but not the name, the matters of Article 8(3)(a), (e), (f), (j) and (k), a summary of the reasons, and any element an Order prescribes; empty for a charity not in the restricted section
GIVEN interp IS AN `Interpretation of Articles 8 to 10` @desc The readings of Articles 8 to 10; the favoured ones apply if left out
      `the registered charity` IS A `Registered charity` @desc What the register holds about the charity, with its standing on the register
      `the required steps notices served` IS A LIST OF `Required steps notice` @desc Every required steps notice served on the charity or on a governor of it; empty if none
      facts IS A `Facts for the public elements (Article 9(1))` @desc Whether a summary of the reasons has been produced to the Commissioner's satisfaction, and whether an Order prescribes another element
GIVETH A LIST OF `Element of the restricted section (Article 9(1))`
`Art 9(1) the public elements of the restricted section` interp `the registered charity` `the required steps notices served` facts MEANS
    IF `the registered charity`'s entity's `standing on the register` EQUALS `entered in the restricted section`
    THEN filter present (LIST `the registration number, but not the registered name`                                -- (a)
                           , `the note of status registered under Article 8(3)(a)`                                 -- (b)
                           , `the registered charitable purposes registered under Article 8(3)(e)`                 -- (b)
                           , `the registered public benefit statement registered under Article 8(3)(f)`            -- (b)
                           , `the note of the annual return registered under Article 8(3)(j)`                      -- (b)
                           , `the note of a required steps notice registered under Article 8(3)(k)`                -- (b)
                           , `a summary of the reasons for registration in the restricted section`                 -- (c)
                           , `another element prescribed by the Minister by Order`)                                -- (d)
    ELSE EMPTY
    WHERE
        present element MEANS
            CONSIDER element
            WHEN `the note of a required steps notice registered under Article 8(3)(k)` THEN NOT null (`Art 8(3)(k) the required steps notices to be noted` interp `the required steps notices served`)
            WHEN `a summary of the reasons for registration in the restricted section` THEN facts's `a summary of the reasons has been produced by the charity to the satisfaction of the Commissioner`
            WHEN `another element prescribed by the Minister by Order` THEN facts's `an Order under Article 9(1)(d) prescribes another element`
            OTHERWISE TRUE

-- Whether a matter entered on the register is one of the public elements of the restricted section: the number is, the name is not (9(1)(a)), the five matters of 9(1)(b) are,
-- the summary of 9(1)(c) is, an element an Order prescribes under 9(1)(d) is, and no other matter is (in particular no item of the historic section, which is not in the restricted section).
@ref Article 9(1) (src:255-259)
@export Whether a matter entered on the register is a public element of the restricted section (Article 9(1)): the registration number is, the registered name is not
GIVEN matter IS A `Matter entered on the register` @desc The matter: the registered name, the registration number, an item of Article 8(3) or 8(5), the summary of the reasons, or an element an Order prescribes
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Art 9(1) the matter is a public element of the restricted section` matter MEANS
    CONSIDER matter
    WHEN `the registered name` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `the registration number` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `an item required by Article 8(3)` item THEN
        CONSIDER item
        WHEN `a note of the status of the entity` THEN TRUE
        WHEN `the registered charitable purposes` THEN TRUE
        WHEN `the registered public benefit statement` THEN TRUE
        WHEN `whether the charity has or has not sent its annual return for the most recent year` THEN TRUE
        WHEN `a note of a required steps notice and of the date on which it was served` THEN TRUE
        OTHERWISE FALSE
    WHEN `the summary of the reasons for registration, produced by the charity` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `an item required by Article 8(5)` item THEN FALSE
    WHEN `another element prescribed by an Order under Article 9(1)(d)` THEN TRUE

-- src:259 | (d) any other element that may be prescribed by the Minister by Order.
@ref Article 9(1)(d) (src:259)
@export The Minister may by Order prescribe other elements of the restricted section that are public (Article 9(1)(d))
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Legal actor` `Act in relation to the register`
`Art 9(1)(d) the Minister may by Order prescribe other elements of the restricted section that are public` MEANS
    `the Minister may by Order prescribe` `other elements of the restricted section that are public`

§§ `Article 9(2): who may request entry in the restricted section`

-- F3.12.  "An applicant for registration, or a charity registered in the general section of the register, may request ... if (a) the applicant meets the funding condition ... or (b) the applicant meets
-- any other condition".  The condition and the Order are inputs: whether the funding condition (or another) is met is a fact the caller supplies.
@ref Article 9(2) (fork F3.12)
GIVEN `the entity` IS AN Entity
      `the funding condition prescribed under Article 9(2)(a) is met` IS A BOOLEAN
      `another condition prescribed under Article 9(2)(b) is met` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`F3.12 reading A: whoever makes the request, an applicant for registration or a registered charity` `the entity` `the funding condition prescribed under Article 9(2)(a) is met` `another condition prescribed under Article 9(2)(b) is met` MEANS
        (   `the entity`'s `standing on the register` EQUALS `an applicant for registration`
         OR `the entity`'s `standing on the register` EQUALS `entered in the general section`)
    AND (`the funding condition prescribed under Article 9(2)(a) is met` OR `another condition prescribed under Article 9(2)(b) is met`)

@ref Article 9(2) (fork F3.12)
GIVEN `the entity` IS AN Entity
      `the funding condition prescribed under Article 9(2)(a) is met` IS A BOOLEAN
      `another condition prescribed under Article 9(2)(b) is met` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`F3.12 reading B: only an applicant for registration` `the entity` `the funding condition prescribed under Article 9(2)(a) is met` `another condition prescribed under Article 9(2)(b) is met` MEANS
        `the entity`'s `standing on the register` EQUALS `an applicant for registration`
    AND (`the funding condition prescribed under Article 9(2)(a) is met` OR `another condition prescribed under Article 9(2)(b) is met`)

-- src:260 | (2) An applicant for registration, or a charity registered in the general section of the register, may request entry in the restricted section of the register if –
-- src:261 | (a) the applicant meets the funding condition, prescribed by the Minister by Order for this purpose, as to refraining from soliciting donations from the general public or from any prescribed description of persons; or
-- src:262 | (b) the applicant meets any other condition that may be prescribed by the Minister by Order, whether by reference to any other source of the entity’s funds or on any other basis.
@ref Article 9(2) (src:260-262)
@export Whether an entity may request entry in the restricted section (Article 9(2)): it is an applicant for registration or a charity in the general section, and meets the funding condition or another condition prescribed by Order
GIVEN interp IS AN `Interpretation of Articles 8 to 10` @desc The readings of Articles 8 to 10 (whether a registered charity may meet the condition); the favoured ones apply if left out
      `the entity` IS AN Entity @desc The entity making the request, with its standing on the register
      `the funding condition prescribed under Article 9(2)(a) is met` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the entity meets the funding condition (refraining from soliciting donations from the general public or from a prescribed description of persons) that an Order prescribes
      `another condition prescribed under Article 9(2)(b) is met` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the entity meets any other condition an Order prescribes
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Art 9(2) the request for entry in the restricted section may be made` interp `the entity` `the funding condition prescribed under Article 9(2)(a) is met` `another condition prescribed under Article 9(2)(b) is met` MEANS
    CONSIDER interp's `who must meet a condition under Article 9(2)`
    WHEN `whoever makes the request, an applicant for registration or a registered charity` THEN
        `F3.12 reading A: whoever makes the request, an applicant for registration or a registered charity` `the entity` `the funding condition prescribed under Article 9(2)(a) is met` `another condition prescribed under Article 9(2)(b) is met`
    WHEN `only an applicant for registration` THEN
        `F3.12 reading B: only an applicant for registration` `the entity` `the funding condition prescribed under Article 9(2)(a) is met` `another condition prescribed under Article 9(2)(b) is met`

-- src:261 | (a) the applicant meets the funding condition, prescribed by the Minister by Order for this purpose, as to refraining from soliciting donations from the general public or from any prescribed description of persons; or
@ref Article 9(2)(a) (src:261)
@export The Minister may by Order prescribe the funding condition for entry in the restricted section (Article 9(2)(a))
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Legal actor` `Act in relation to the register`
`Art 9(2)(a) the Minister may by Order prescribe the funding condition for entry in the restricted section` MEANS
    `the Minister may by Order prescribe` `the funding condition for entry in the restricted section`

-- src:262 | (b) the applicant meets any other condition that may be prescribed by the Minister by Order, whether by reference to any other source of the entity’s funds or on any other basis.
@ref Article 9(2)(b) (src:262)
@export The Minister may by Order prescribe other conditions for entry in the restricted section (Article 9(2)(b))
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Legal actor` `Act in relation to the register`
`Art 9(2)(b) the Minister may by Order prescribe other conditions for entry in the restricted section` MEANS
    `the Minister may by Order prescribe` `other conditions for entry in the restricted section`

§§ `Article 9(3): what the Order must contain`

-- src:264 | (a) must prescribe grounds, that may include the exercise of discretion by the Commissioner, on which the Commissioner may accept or refuse such a request;
@ref Article 9(3)(a) (src:264)
GIVEN content IS A `Content of an Order under Article 9`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Art 9(3)(a) the Order prescribes grounds on which the Commissioner may accept or refuse a request` content MEANS
    content's `prescribes grounds on which the Commissioner may accept or refuse a request`

-- src:266 | (i) what constitutes soliciting,
@ref Article 9(3)(b)(i) (src:266)
GIVEN content IS A `Content of an Order under Article 9`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Art 9(3)(b)(i) the Order specifies what constitutes soliciting` content MEANS
    content's `specifies what constitutes soliciting`

-- src:267 | (ii) what constitutes a donation, and
@ref Article 9(3)(b)(ii) (src:267)
GIVEN content IS A `Content of an Order under Article 9`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Art 9(3)(b)(ii) the Order specifies what constitutes a donation` content MEANS
    content's `specifies what constitutes a donation`

-- (iii) is required only "if the Order does not prescribe a description of persons".
-- src:268 | (iii) if the Order does not prescribe a description of persons, what constitutes the general public for the purpose of the Order; and
@ref Article 9(3)(b)(iii) (src:268)
GIVEN content IS A `Content of an Order under Article 9`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Art 9(3)(b)(iii) the Order specifies what constitutes the general public, where it prescribes no description of persons` content MEANS
    content's `prescribes a description of persons` OR content's `specifies what constitutes the general public`

-- src:265 | (b) must specify, for the purpose of paragraph (2)(a) –
@ref Article 9(3)(b) (src:265)
GIVEN content IS A `Content of an Order under Article 9`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Art 9(3)(b) the Order specifies, for the purpose of paragraph (2)(a), what soliciting, a donation and the general public are` content MEANS
        `Art 9(3)(b)(i) the Order specifies what constitutes soliciting` content
    AND `Art 9(3)(b)(ii) the Order specifies what constitutes a donation` content
    AND `Art 9(3)(b)(iii) the Order specifies what constitutes the general public, where it prescribes no description of persons` content

-- "may make provision under sub-paragraph (b) by reference to the exercise of discretion by the Commissioner, or in any other manner": a permission about the content of the Order, which
-- excludes nothing, so a provision of either manner is within the Article.
-- src:269 | (c) may make provision under sub-paragraph (b) by reference to the exercise of discretion by the Commissioner, or in any other manner.
@ref Article 9(3)(c) (src:269)
GIVEN `the provision refers to the exercise of discretion by the Commissioner` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Art 9(3)(c) a provision under sub-paragraph (b) of that manner is permitted` `the provision refers to the exercise of discretion by the Commissioner` MEANS
    TRUE

-- src:263 | (3) The Order –
-- src:264 | (a) must prescribe grounds, that may include the exercise of discretion by the Commissioner, on which the Commissioner may accept or refuse such a request;
-- src:265 | (b) must specify, for the purpose of paragraph (2)(a) –
-- src:266 | (i) what constitutes soliciting,
-- src:267 | (ii) what constitutes a donation, and
-- src:268 | (iii) if the Order does not prescribe a description of persons, what constitutes the general public for the purpose of the Order; and
-- src:269 | (c) may make provision under sub-paragraph (b) by reference to the exercise of discretion by the Commissioner, or in any other manner.
@ref Article 9(3) (src:263-269)
@export Whether the Order under Article 9 contains what Article 9(3) requires: grounds for accepting or refusing a request, and what soliciting, a donation and (where no description of persons is prescribed) the general public are
GIVEN content IS A `Content of an Order under Article 9` @desc What the Order contains: grounds, the meaning of soliciting and of a donation, whether it prescribes a description of persons, and the meaning of the general public
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Art 9(3) the Order contains what Article 9(3) requires` content MEANS
        `Art 9(3)(a) the Order prescribes grounds on which the Commissioner may accept or refuse a request` content
    AND `Art 9(3)(b) the Order specifies, for the purpose of paragraph (2)(a), what soliciting, a donation and the general public are` content

§§ `Article 9(4) and (5): the request`

-- src:270 | (4) A request under paragraph (2) must be –
-- src:271 | (a) made in the form published by the Commissioner; and
-- src:272 | (b) supported by information and evidence to the satisfaction of the Commissioner.
@ref Article 9(4) (src:270-272)
@export Whether a request for entry in the restricted section is in the form the Commissioner published and is supported by information and evidence to the Commissioner's satisfaction (Article 9(4))
GIVEN request IS A `Request for entry in the restricted section (Article 9)` @desc The request: whether it is in the published form, whether it is supported to the Commissioner's satisfaction, and the statement of intention that goes with it
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Art 9(4) the request is in the published form and supported to the Commissioner's satisfaction` request MEANS
        request's `made in the form published by the Commissioner`
    AND request's `supported by information and evidence to the satisfaction of the Commissioner`

-- The statement must be one of the two intentions that fit the one who requests: for an application, to be treated as withdrawn or as an application for the general section; for a charity in
-- the general section, to remain so registered or to be treated as applying to be deregistered.
-- src:273 | (5) A request under paragraph (2) must be accompanied by a statement of the applicant’s intention, in the event of refusal of the request, being –
-- src:274 | (a) in the case of an application for registration –
-- src:275 | (i) that that application should be treated as withdrawn, or
-- src:276 | (ii) that it should be treated as an application for entry in the general section of the register, on provision of any further information and evidence required for such an application; or
-- src:277 | (b) in the case of a charity registered in the general section of the register –
-- src:278 | (i) that the charity should remain so registered, or
-- src:279 | (ii) that the charity should be treated as applying to be deregistered, on provision of any further information and evidence required for such an application.
@ref Article 9(5) (src:273-279)
@export Whether a request is accompanied by a statement of the applicant's intention on refusal that fits the one who requests (Article 9(5)): an applicant for registration states (a)(i) or (a)(ii); a charity registered in the general section states (b)(i) or (b)(ii)
GIVEN `the entity` IS AN Entity @desc The entity making the request, with its standing on the register
      request IS A `Request for entry in the restricted section (Article 9)` @desc The request, with the statement of intention that accompanies it, if any
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Art 9(5) the request is accompanied by a statement of intention that Article 9(5) allows` `the entity` request MEANS
    CONSIDER request's `accompanied by a statement of the intention`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
    WHEN JUST intention THEN
        CONSIDER `the entity`'s `standing on the register`
        WHEN `an applicant for registration` THEN
            intention EQUALS `that the application should be treated as withdrawn`
            OR intention EQUALS `that the application should be treated as an application for entry in the general section, on provision of any further information and evidence required`
        WHEN `entered in the general section` THEN
            intention EQUALS `that the charity should remain so registered`
            OR intention EQUALS `that the charity should be treated as applying to be deregistered, on provision of any further information and evidence required`
        OTHERWISE FALSE

-- The request complies with paragraphs (4) and (5), as a matter of fact.  Article 9(6)(a) turns on the Commissioner being SATISFIED that it does (an input); this is the fact it is about.
@ref Article 9(4), 9(5) (src:270-279)
@export Whether the request complied with Article 9(4) and (5), as a matter of fact (the fact the Commissioner is to be satisfied of under Article 9(6)(a))
GIVEN `the entity` IS AN Entity @desc The entity making the request, with its standing on the register
      request IS A `Request for entry in the restricted section (Article 9)` @desc The request, with the statement of intention that accompanies it, if any
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Art 9(4) and (5) the request complied` `the entity` request MEANS
        `Art 9(4) the request is in the published form and supported to the Commissioner's satisfaction` request
    AND `Art 9(5) the request is accompanied by a statement of intention that Article 9(5) allows` `the entity` request

§§ `Article 9(6): when the Commissioner may enter the charity in the restricted section`

-- (c): "no ground, prescribed under paragraph (3), on which the request must be refused or, in the case of a discretionary ground, on which the Commissioner considers the request should be refused".
-- src:283 | (c) that there is no ground, prescribed under paragraph (3), on which the request must be refused or, in the case of a discretionary ground, on which the Commissioner considers the request should be refused.
@ref Article 9(6)(c) (src:283)
GIVEN `a ground on which the request must be refused applies` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Commissioner considers the request should be refused on a discretionary ground` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Art 9(6)(c) there is no ground on which the request must be refused or should be refused` `a ground on which the request must be refused applies` `the Commissioner considers the request should be refused on a discretionary ground` MEANS
    NOT (`a ground on which the request must be refused applies` OR `the Commissioner considers the request should be refused on a discretionary ground`)

-- src:280 | (6) The Commissioner must not enter a charity in the restricted section of the register unless satisfied –
-- src:281 | (a) that the request complied with paragraphs (4) and (5);
-- src:282 | (b) that one of the conditions prescribed under paragraph (2) is met; and
-- src:283 | (c) that there is no ground, prescribed under paragraph (3), on which the request must be refused or, in the case of a discretionary ground, on which the Commissioner considers the request should be refused.
@ref Article 9(6) (src:280-283)
@export Whether the Commissioner is satisfied of all three things Article 9(6) requires before entering a charity in the restricted section; each satisfaction is the Commissioner's own state of mind and is supplied
GIVEN satisfaction IS A `Satisfaction of the Commissioner under Article 9(6)` @desc The Commissioner's three satisfactions: that the request complied with Article 9(4) and (5); that one of the conditions prescribed under Article 9(2) is met; that no ground requires or, for a discretionary ground, counsels refusal
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Art 9(6) the Commissioner may enter the charity in the restricted section` satisfaction MEANS
        satisfaction's `satisfied that the request complied with paragraphs (4) and (5)`
    AND satisfaction's `satisfied that one of the conditions prescribed under paragraph (2) is met`
    AND satisfaction's `satisfied that there is no ground on which the request must be refused or, for a discretionary ground, should be refused`

-- The prohibition bites only where the Commissioner is not satisfied of all three; an entry made then is a breach.  The Article states no time, so no WITHIN.
-- src:280 | (6) The Commissioner must not enter a charity in the restricted section of the register unless satisfied –
@ref Article 9(6) (src:280)
@export The Commissioner must not enter a charity in the restricted section unless satisfied of the three things in Article 9(6); a prohibition that bites only where the Commissioner is not so satisfied
GIVEN satisfaction IS A `Satisfaction of the Commissioner under Article 9(6)` @desc The Commissioner's three satisfactions under Article 9(6)(a), (b) and (c)
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Legal actor` `Act in relation to the register`
`Art 9(6) the Commissioner must not enter the charity in the restricted section unless satisfied` satisfaction MEANS
    IF `Art 9(6) the Commissioner may enter the charity in the restricted section` satisfaction
    THEN FULFILLED
    ELSE PARTY `the Commissioner`
         SHANT `enter a charity in the restricted section of the register`
         HENCE FULFILLED
         LEST BREACH BY `the Commissioner` BECAUSE "Article 9(6): the Commissioner entered the charity in the restricted section without being satisfied of all three things"

-- IP27: the Commissioner's decision on a request for the restricted section (consumed by G8, Article 33, and G9, Schedule 1 paragraph 4(3)): its subject, and its outcome.
@ref Article 9(6), 9(7) (src:280-286)
@export The decision of the Commissioner on a request for entry in the restricted section: the subject (Article 9(6) and (7)) and whether the Commissioner did what was asked or refused
GIVEN `the Commissioner enters the charity in the restricted section` IS A BOOLEAN @desc TRUE if the Commissioner granted the request, FALSE if the Commissioner refused it
GIVETH A `Decision of the Commissioner`
`Art 9(6) the decision of the Commissioner on the request for the restricted section` `the Commissioner enters the charity in the restricted section` MEANS
    `Decision of the Commissioner` WITH
        subject IS `whether to enter a charity in the restricted section, Article 9(6) and (7)`
        outcome IS IF `the Commissioner enters the charity in the restricted section`
                   THEN `the Commissioner does what was sought or proposed`
                   ELSE `the Commissioner refuses`

§§ `Article 9(7): a refusal`

-- The Article states no time within which the notice is to be given: no WITHIN is written (and none is invented).
-- src:284 | (7) If the Commissioner refuses a request, he or she –
-- src:285 | (a) must give written notice of the refusal to the applicant or charity; and
@ref Article 9(7)(a) (src:284-285)
@export If the Commissioner refuses a request, the Commissioner must give written notice of the refusal to the applicant or charity (Article 9(7)(a)); no time is stated
GIVEN `the Commissioner refuses the request` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Commissioner has refused the request
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Legal actor` `Act in relation to the register`
`Art 9(7)(a) the Commissioner must give written notice of the refusal` `the Commissioner refuses the request` MEANS
    IF `the Commissioner refuses the request`
    THEN PARTY `the Commissioner`
         MUST `give written notice of the refusal of a request`
         HENCE FULFILLED
         LEST BREACH BY `the Commissioner` BECAUSE "Article 9(7)(a): written notice of the refusal was not given to the applicant or charity"
    ELSE FULFILLED

-- What proceeding on the intention does, limb by limb (Article 9(5)).
-- src:273 | (5) A request under paragraph (2) must be accompanied by a statement of the applicant’s intention, in the event of refusal of the request, being –
-- src:274 | (a) in the case of an application for registration –
-- src:275 | (i) that that application should be treated as withdrawn, or
-- src:276 | (ii) that it should be treated as an application for entry in the general section of the register, on provision of any further information and evidence required for such an application; or
-- src:277 | (b) in the case of a charity registered in the general section of the register –
-- src:278 | (i) that the charity should remain so registered, or
-- src:279 | (ii) that the charity should be treated as applying to be deregistered, on provision of any further information and evidence required for such an application.
@ref Article 9(7)(b), 9(5) (src:273-279)
@export What follows if the Commissioner proceeds on the intention stated with a refused request (Article 9(7)(b) with 9(5)): withdrawn, treated as an application for the general section, remains registered, or treated as applying to be deregistered (Article 15)
GIVEN intention IS AN `Intention stated with a request (Article 9(5))` @desc The intention the applicant or charity stated with the request
GIVETH A `Consequence of proceeding on the intention stated with a request (Article 9(7)(b))`
`Art 9(7)(b) the consequence of proceeding on the intention` intention MEANS
    CONSIDER intention
    WHEN `that the application should be treated as withdrawn` THEN `the application is treated as withdrawn`
    WHEN `that the application should be treated as an application for entry in the general section, on provision of any further information and evidence required` THEN
        `the application is treated as an application for entry in the general section, on provision of any further information and evidence required`
    WHEN `that the charity should remain so registered` THEN `the charity remains registered in the general section`
    WHEN `that the charity should be treated as applying to be deregistered, on provision of any further information and evidence required` THEN
        `the charity is treated as applying to be deregistered, on provision of any further information and evidence required`

-- src:286 | (b) may proceed on the basis of the intention stated under paragraph (5).
@ref Article 9(7)(b) (src:286)
@export If the Commissioner refuses a request, the Commissioner may proceed on the basis of the intention stated with it (Article 9(7)(b)); a permission, so not proceeding is no breach
GIVEN `the Commissioner refuses the request` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Commissioner has refused the request
      intention IS AN `Intention stated with a request (Article 9(5))` @desc The intention the applicant or charity stated with the request
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Legal actor` `Act in relation to the register`
`Art 9(7)(b) the Commissioner may proceed on the intention stated with the request` `the Commissioner refuses the request` intention MEANS
    IF `the Commissioner refuses the request`
    THEN PARTY `the Commissioner`
         MAY `proceed on the basis of the intention stated with the request` intention
         HENCE FULFILLED
    ELSE FULFILLED
